Reversing the order of words while normalising spaces:

```python
line = "  the sky  is blue "
words = line.split()               # ['the', 'sky', 'is', 'blue']
print(" ".join(reversed(words)))   # blue is sky the
```

The same parsing in C++, where `>>` also skips any amount of whitespace:

```cpp
